{"name":"Black Fox","hex":"#4f4842","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black fox","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of silver fox, especially in reference to foxskin.","Synonym of Blanford's fox"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black_fox"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silver fox (animal)","blocks":[{"text":"The silver fox, sometimes referred to as the black fox, or blue fox, is a melanistic form of the red fox. Silver foxes display a great deal of pelt variation. Some are completely glossy black except for a white colouration on the tip of the tail, giving them a somewhat silvery appearance. Some silver foxes are bluish-grey, and some may have a cinereous colour on the sides."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Silberfuchs_08.jpg/330px-Silberfuchs_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_fox_(animal)","wikidata":"Q2574250"},{"title":"Black Fox (Cherokee chief)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Fox, also called Enola, was a Cherokee leader during the Cherokee–American wars. He was a signatory of the Holston Treaty, and later became a Principal Chief of the Cherokee Nation."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Fox_(Cherokee_chief)","wikidata":"Q51751"},{"title":"Fox","blocks":[{"text":"Foxes are small-to-medium-sized omnivorous mammals belonging to several genera of the family Canidae. They have a flattened skull; upright, triangular ears; a pointed, slightly upturned snout; and a long, bushy tail (\"brush\")."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Vulpes_vulpes_ssp_fulvus.jpg/330px-Vulpes_vulpes_ssp_fulvus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fox","wikidata":"Q8331"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Silberfuchs_06.jpg/500px-Silberfuchs_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Silberfuchs_06.jpg/1280px-Silberfuchs_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Silberfuchs_06.jpg/500px-Silberfuchs_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An adult silver fox","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilberfuchs_06.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Fur_silverfox.jpg/330px-Fur_silverfox.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Fur_silverfox.jpg/330px-Fur_silverfox.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Silver fox furs","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFur_silverfox.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Feeding_the_silver_foxes_%28c_1901%29.jpg/500px-Feeding_the_silver_foxes_%28c_1901%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam